    "finding": "Scored with the gate's own statistic, GT poses sit at 18.89, 22.00, 12.59, 8.58, 11.69 (mean per scenario), one to two orders of magnitude above tau = 2.5, while the same GT poses against the analytic arena give 0.0054. Geometry is therefore self-consistent and the error lives in the local plane fit. On density: the 1500-point budget scores 14.749 and the 20000-point budget 13.612 (scenario means), so the score DOES move with the requested budget; but the reference returned at 20000 and 200000 is identical, and the production estimator truncates every reference to 600.0 points before the k-NN plane fit. Raising the budget above ~600 is arithmetically incapable of changing the result, so 'density is not the cause' is NOT supported: what the sweep excludes is only that budgets above 20000 matter in this simulator.",
    "second_finding": "The analytic value must NOT be read as 'the gate passes'. This simulator is effectively noise-free (0.01 m sampling jitter against sigma = 0.12 m), so the NIS scale carries no physical meaning. It means the simulator is not a valid test bed, not that the candidate is good.",
